OTP application refuses the command outright with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0x6985"},{"type":"text","text":" rather than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"waiting, so the stream yields "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/YubiOTP\/Status\/finished(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" alone and cancellation does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing. Python and Java accept the same parameters on their SmartCard backends and likewise"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ignore them."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This is a limitation of the application, not of SmartCard: an application that defines a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"continuation on top of APDUs can report progress and be cancelled over the same transport.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"CTAP2 does exactly that — it answers ","type":"text"},{"code":"0x9100","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the host polls with ","type":"text"},{"code":"NFCCTAP_GETRESPONSE","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which is how ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/CTAP2\/Status\/waitingForUser(cancel:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" works over NFC. YubiOTP defines no such","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exchange.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Important"},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Requires ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/YubiOTP\/Feature\/challengeResponse","type":"reference"},{"text":", available on YubiKey 2.2 or later.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Performs an HMAC-SHA1 challenge-response against a slot.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"metad